🛒 Retail Sales Data Analysis
📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing transactional retail data to uncover meaningful business insights related to:

Revenue performance

Product demand

Customer value

Geographic sales distribution

Using Python-based data analysis libraries, the dataset is cleaned, transformed, and analyzed to support data-driven business decision-making.

🎯 Objective

The primary objective of this project is to:

Evaluate overall sales performance

Identify key drivers of revenue

Discover top-performing products

Identify high-value customers

Analyze country-wise sales distribution

Calculate Average Order Value (AOV)

🛠️ Technologies Used

Python

Pandas – Data cleaning & transformation

NumPy – Numerical operations

Matplotlib – Data visualization

Seaborn – Advanced visualizations

📂 Dataset Description
The link to the dataset is as follow,
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mashlyn/online-retail-ii-uci
The dataset contains retail transactional data including:

Invoice Number

Product Description

Quantity

Unit Price

Customer ID

Country

🔄 Data Cleaning Steps

Removed cancelled transactions

Removed missing/null values

Created a new column: Total Sales = Quantity × Unit Price

Ensured proper data types for analysis

📊 Key Analysis Performed
1️⃣ Total Revenue

Calculated overall revenue generated from all valid transactions.

2️⃣ Top-Selling Products

Identified products generating the highest revenue.

3️⃣ Top Customers

Found high-value customers contributing the most revenue.

4️⃣ Country-Wise Sales Analysis

Analyzed revenue distribution across different countries.

5️⃣ Average Order Value (AOV)

Calculated the average revenue per order to measure business performance.

📈 Business Insights

This project helps businesses:

Understand revenue trends

Identify profitable products

Recognize loyal and high-value customers

Make strategic pricing and inventory decisions

Optimize geographic sales strategies

🚀 How to Run the Project

Clone this repository:

git clone https://github.com/your-username/retail-sales-analysis.git

Navigate to the project folder:

cd retail-sales-analysis

Install required libraries:

pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn

Run the Python script or Jupyter Notebook.

